abstract: >-
  A formal audit, by the author of the candidate theory Q, of how far a categorical
  unification of theories of consciousness (IIT, GNWT, attention schema theory) and of
  frameworks brought to bear on it (FEP, quantum Darwinism) can go, for structural proxies
  of the theories, with the unity-sufficiency obligation of Q as test case, in three acts:
  negative delimitation, a Gaussian laboratory (exact in two units, numerical in four), and
  a positive route through intervention monotonicity, which is a declared weakening of the
  order clause of Q, not its unity sufficiency. Results are labelled by evidence: Lean 4
  proofs, paper proofs, exact computation (SymPy and exact integer enumeration) and
  numerical illustration. Q is neither
  demonstrated nor refuted. The archive contains the paper, seven Lean 4 files checked
  without Mathlib, a Lean 4 project with Mathlib of eight modules that checks three analytic
  results on J (the connectivity lemma, the min-cut sandwich and the scaling proposition) and
  the exact frontier of intervention monotonicity with real-valued degrees, twelve Python
  scripts with their expected outputs, and verification scripts. Version 1.1; the changes
  from version 1.0 are listed in CHANGES.md.
